---
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import Doc from '../../layouts/Doc.astro';
import { counts, publishedVersion, sourceUnreleased, version } from '../../lib/catalog.mjs';
---

<Doc
  frontmatter={{
    title: 'Release notes',
    description: 'The website follows the version and catalogs in the just-vibe package.',
  }}
>
  <h2>Current package: {publishedVersion}</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={`https://www.npmjs.com/package/just-vibe/v/${publishedVersion}`}>
      View v{publishedVersion} on npm <Icon name="arrow-up-right" />
    </a>
  </p>
  {sourceUnreleased && (
    <p>
      The source is at {version}, which is not published yet. Install commands and the release manifest
      use {publishedVersion}.
    </p>
  )}
  <p>
    The current catalog includes <strong>{counts.commands} skill names</strong> ({counts.workflows}{' '}
    workflows and {counts.commands - counts.workflows} aliases),{' '}
    <strong>{counts.profiles} role profiles</strong>, and{' '}
    <strong>{counts.packs} specialist packs</strong>.
  </p>
  <h2>New in 0.12.0</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Agent QA derives acceptance criteria from the request and checks them in a real browser, with screenshots, stale-evidence detection and retained failure and retest history.</li>
    <li>A local preference dashboard edits, previews, disables and restores preferences with provenance and revision checks, plus task exclusions and project-context backup and import.</li>
    <li>Delivery diagnosis reports which hook, workflow and tool stages were observed, with opt-in live host journeys.</li>
    <li>Release metadata for the website and portfolio consumers is generated from the canonical catalog.</li>
    <li>Windows path and shim handling, and dashboard, QA and recovery fixes from review.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>New in 0.11.0</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Reprompt improves a supplied prompt and can incorporate relevant available skills.</li>
    <li>All installed Claude commands support /jv and /just-vibe dispatchers, plus both colon namespaces.</li>
    <li>Owned shortcut installation, selective-pack support, update checks and edited-file protection.</li>
    <li>Runtime, process-cleanup, Unicode, Git-index and recovery fixes from two complete code reviews.</li>
  </ul>
  <p><a href="/docs/command-shortcuts/">Read the command shortcut guide and host differences.</a></p>
  <h2>Previously in 0.10.0</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Persistent goals, scoped memory, session imports, orchestration and reviewed worker changes.
    </li>
    <li>43 focused technical methods, 24 specialist agents and 22 connector recipes.</li>
    <li>
      Trusted runners, bounded jobs and services, monitoring, evaluation receipts and a local
      operator board.
    </li>
    <li>
      Additional editor adapters, a private plan canvas and pinned installation updates with
      rollback.
    </li>
    <li>
      Privacy, cancellation, concurrent-write and crash-recovery fixes backed by regression tests.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Execution and optional integrations require explicit setup and trust. Live host, provider and
    operating-system coverage remains distinct from local fixture results.
    <a href="/docs/workbench/">Read the workbench guide.</a>
  </p>
  <h2>Previously in 0.9.0</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Workflow selection and tool-discovery guidance from ordinary requests.</li>
    <li>
      Project and personal feedback with version history, rollback, retirement and forgetting.
    </li>
    <li>
      Task recovery after compaction, evidence freshness checks and bounded completion reminders.
    </li>
    <li>Updated documentation, page transitions, spacing and SVG interface icons.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Automatic activation requires supported native hooks and the host's hook trust. After updating,
    review the plugin hooks and start a new conversation.{' '}
    <a href="/docs/automatic/">Read the automatic assistance guide.</a>
  </p>
  <h2>Previously in the 0.8 series</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Intent workflows for durable memory, working alternatives, requirement evidence, exercises,
      experiment comparison, and selective task undo.
    </li>
    <li>Command-specific technical guidance, scope, and verification contracts.</li>
    <li>
      Conversation and teaching guidance for clearer explanations, useful context recovery, and
      focused clarifications.
    </li>
    <li>Runtime and output-handling fixes, with targeted tests and release checks.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Update an existing installation</h2>
  <div class="code-block">
    <code>pnpm dlx just-vibe@latest update</code>
  </div>
  <p>
    Append <code>--target claude</code> for Claude Code, then start a new conversation.{' '}
    <a href="/docs/updates/">See the update guide.</a>
  </p>
  <p>
    The npm package includes CHANGELOG.md with the complete package change history. Website updates
    can ship independently of the CLI version.
  </p>
</Doc>
